.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH taur-ssh-auth 1  "taur-ssh-auth " 
.SH NAME
taur\-ssh\-auth \- OpenSSH `AuthorizedKeysCommand`: `taur ssh\-auth %t %k`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaur ssh\-auth\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIKEY_TYPE\fR> <\fIKEY\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
OpenSSH `AuthorizedKeysCommand`: `taur ssh\-auth %t %k`.
.PP
Prints one `authorized_keys` line forcing `taur git\-serve` when the key is registered, or nothing (exit 0) when it is not.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
Data directory (default: ~/.local/share/taur)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<DB>\fR
SQLite database path (default: <home>/taur.db)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIKEY_TYPE\fR>
Key type offered by the client (`%t`)
.TP
<\fIKEY\fR>
Base64 key blob offered by the client (`%k`)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Command\-line flags take precedence over environment variables, which take precedence over defaults.
.TP
\fBTAUR_HOME\fR
Data directory (git repos, outbox, SSH host key; default database). Default: ~/.local/share/taur.
.TP
\fBTAUR_DB\fR
SQLite database file. WAL and SHM sidecars are created beside it. The parent directory must already exist. Default: <home>/taur.db.
